/-!
# (III-b′): the zone geometry of a later line of Lemma 7.6's retained continuation

Packet PROVE-RETAUX79B (PROVE-RETAUX79's "What remains" R1; PROVE-DOMAINMARKOV8 §2 (III-b)). At a disjoint pair
`(a, b)` (`Sec7.Lemma76G.IsSetting`) the retained chart `(φ₀, ψ₀)` reads the boundary data of the field as the zone word
`β₀ = ((zoneData φ₀ α a β b).word c₀ g₁ g₂ g₃ g₄).trunc` (LEMMA76G). The continuation of the second path after `b` is a
flow line of angle `θ` in this chart: its force word is the flow-line word of `β₀` at the seed `0`
(`flowLineXL/XR/RhoL/RhoR β₀.fn β₀.jumps 0 θ`), its chart path `γ` is generated by a continuous driver `W`, and at a
later line `b' ≥ b` (capacity time `Q`) the retained chart `(φ₁, ψ₁)` is the stop-line chart followed by the centred
Loewner map `f_Q` ((III-a): `ψ₁ = ψ₀ ∘ f_Q⁻¹` on `ℍ`, `RetAux79.retChart_trans_of_image`). This file proves the
pointwise boundary-data identity (III-b′): off a finite set,

`forceBoundaryData κ ρL ρR (V^L_Q − W_Q) (V^R_Q − W_Q) = β_t.fn + θχ`,

with `V^R_Q = rightImg W (x^R) Q`, `V^L_Q = −rightImg (−W) (−x^L) Q` the geometric images of the marks and
`β_t = ((zoneData φ₁ α a β b').word c₀ g₁ g₂ g₃ g₄).trunc` the zone word of the later line, `g₁ = −λ − θχ`,
`g₂ = λ − θχ`.

## Proof

* **Word facts in one setting** (`fn_zword_*`): off the six zone points, the zone word is `g₁`/`g₂` at chart points on
  the left/right of the second tip `0` that the inverse chart sends to the second prefix, `g₃`/`g₄` at those
  left/right of the first tip sent to the first prefix, and the original datum `c₀.fn p` at the chart point of an
  untouched real `p`.
* **Transport of real points** (`inv₁_eq_inv₀_of_isForwardSol`): if the real point `x` of the stop-line chart has a
  forward solution `u` up to `Q`, then `ψ₁(u_Q) = ψ₀(x)` (`f_Q` is continuous at `x` from `ℍ`, `ψ₀`, `ψ₁` are
  continuous on `ℍ̄`).
* **Untouched points stay untouched and are alive** (`exists_isForwardSol_chartPt`): an untouched real point `p` of the
  later line is untouched at the stop line, its stop-line chart point `T₀(p)` is off the chart path, nonzero and in the
  closure of `ℍ \ K_Q`, hence alive (`GB7a.exists_isForwardSol_of_mem_closure`), and `T₁(p) = f_Q(T₀(p))`.
* **Alive points are off the chart path** (`ne_trace_of_isForwardSol`): GB6's `not_isForwardSol_of_tip` at every
  time `s ≤ Q`.
* **Real flow** (`exists_alive_gImg_eq`, counting lemmas): every `y > R̃ = rightImg W 0 Q − W_Q` is `f_Q(x)` for an
  alive `x > 0`; the right marks `≤ y` after the flow are the marks `≤ x` before; below `R̃` there is none (mirror on
  the left).
* **Assembly** (`forceBoundaryData_eq_zword_add`): for `y > R̃` the force datum at `y` is the stop-line force datum at
  `x` (`= β₀.fn x + θχ`, `Exist.forceBoundaryData_flowLine_seed`) and `β_t.fn y = β₀.fn x` by the word facts and the
  transport (the first tip moves to `f_Q(M₁)`); on `(0, R̃)` both sides are `λ` (`R̃ ≤ R₂'`); mirror on the left.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

noncomputable section

open Complex Set Filter Topology
open scoped NNReal ENNReal

open QuantumZipper (H Hbar fwdMap fwdMapInv fwdHull)

namespace InteractingSLE

namespace Restart.RetAux79

